Hi, bumping the thread for vote. Thanks, Sahil

On Tue, Apr 28, 2026 at 1:07=E2=80=AFPM Sahil Devgon <sahildevgon.30@gmail.=
com>
wrote:

> Thanks for the vote! We have 2 (+1 binding : Chia-Ping and Omnia ) and 1
> (+1 non-binding: Vaquar) votes so far for the KIP.
>
> *Quick Summary:*
> The KIP proposes *exposing all 7 metrics from /proc/self/io* instead of
> the current 2 (*read_bytes and write_bytes*) with the *5 additional*
> metrics (*rchar, wchar, syscr, syscw, cancelled_write_bytes*) that would
> enable operators to diagnose *cache effectiveness, write amplification,
> and I/O pattern inefficiencies *directly from Kafka's JMX.
> The change is purely additive and backward compatible.
>
> KIP-1291 : https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/co48G
> DISCUSS thread:
> https://lists.apache.org/thread/o6tlkz2r32f1c7db5b2mxzl335sodwng
> VOTE thread:
> https://lists.apache.org/thread/dllnl649lj2qsr2myqcm6s80vc4gkmzn
>
> I would request the rest of the community members to review and vote, and
> if there are still more suggestions and a need for discussion I am open t=
o
> it.
>
> Best,
> Sahil Devgon
>
>
> On Mon, Apr 27, 2026 at 4:02=E2=80=AFPM Omnia Ibrahim <o.g.h.ibrahim@gmai=
l.com>
