Hello Ivan and all, I just want to give a quick update and answer a
few pending questions.

AS8: The AuthorizedOperations is back in DescribeMirrors
request/response schemas and I learned something new.

---

RS4: The design has been updated since my previous answer. Here is the
current state.

The mirror fetcher now uses READ_UNCOMMITTED, so it replicates records
up to the log end offset on the source, including ongoing transaction
records. This reduces steady-state replication lag compared to the
previous READ_COMMITTED approach. On failover, any ongoing transaction
is aborted.

---

JR10: We have the mirror.groups.include and mirror.groups.exclude
properties, so users can fully customize the behavior here.

JR11: Thanks for raising. We have a solution for this issue. We will
update the KIP soon.

JR12: This is an oversight. MirrorMetadataManager does not handle
topology changes. KIP updated.

JR14: Yes, the KIP was recently updated as you say.

JR15: Correct. Do you think that we should have dedicated
configurations for cluster mirroring and avoid sharing with
intra-cluster replication?

JR16: LME (last mirror epoch) is stored in __mirror_state internal topic.

JR17: Thanks for raising. When stop mirroring is triggered, ongoing
transactions are aborted, preserving all previously committed data.
More details in EOS paragraph.

JR19: Yes, new topics matching the regex are automatically discovered
and created on the destination. The include/exclude regex patterns are
stored as mirror-level configs (MIRROR resource type in cluster
metadata), not as topic-level configs.

The MirrorCoordinator runs a periodic metadata refresh task that
fetches all topic metadata from the source cluster, matches topics
against the include/exclude patterns, and identifies ones not yet
mirrored. For each newly discovered topic, it sends a
CreateTopicsRequest to the destination controller (preserving the
source topic UUID) and then sets the mirror.name topic-level config on
the newly created topic.

---

IY1: We are still discussing a few solution strategies and
improvements around this. We will update the KIP soon.

IY2: You are right. I did an update to the very beginning of the
proposed changes section to define the cluster mirror entity before
moving on with the architecture components descriptions. Let me know
if it makes sense.

Thanks
Fede

