an.jira.plugin.system.issuetabpanels:all-tabpanel ]

Bill Bejeck resolved KAFKA-15768.
---------------------------------
    Resolution: Fixed

> StateQueryResult#getOnlyPartitionResult should not throw for FailedQueryR=
esult
> -------------------------------------------------------------------------=
-----
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-15768
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-15768
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Bug
>          Components: streams
>            Reporter: Matthias J. Sax
>            Assignee: Gavin Wang
>            Priority: Major
>             Fix For: 4.4.0
>
>
> Calling `StateQueryResult#getOnlyPartitionResult` crashes with an incorre=
ct `IllegalArgumentException` if any result is a `FailedQueryResult` (and e=
ven if there is only a single FailedQueryResult).
> The issue is the internal `filter(r -> r.getResult() !=3D 0)` step, that =
blindly (and incorrectly) calls `getResult`.
> Given the semantics of `getOnlyPartitionResult` we should not care if the=
 result is SuccessQueryResult or FailedQueryResult, but only check if there=
 is a single result or not. (The user has no means to avoid getting the und=
erlying error otherwise.)
> Side-note: why does `FailedQueryResult#getResult` throw an IllegalArgumen=
tException (there is no argument passed into the method =E2=80=93 it should=
 rather be an `IllegalStateException` =E2=80=93 but I guess we would need a=
 KIP for this fix?)



