Subject: [jira] [Created] (KAFKA-20552) Support log segments larger than 2
 GB
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable
X-JIRA-FingerPrint: 30527f35849b9dde25b450d4833f0394
From: "Haifeng Chen (Jira)" <jira@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Haifeng Chen created KAFKA-20552:
------------------------------------

             Summary: Support log segments larger than 2 GB
                 Key: KAFKA-20552
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20552
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Improvement
          Components: core
            Reporter: Haifeng Chen


The=C2=A0{{log.segment.bytes}}=C2=A0broker config (and its topic-level syno=
nym=C2=A0{{{}segment.bytes{}}}) is currently defined as=C2=A0{{{}ConfigDef.=
Type.INT{}}}, capping the maximum segment size at=C2=A0{{Integer.MAX_VALUE}=
}=C2=A0(2,147,483,647 bytes, ~2 GB). Additionally, the=C2=A0{{.index}}=C2=
=A0file format stores physical file positions as 4-byte signed integers, wh=
ich also cannot address beyond ~2 GB.

With modern storage hardware (multi-TB NVMe drives) and high-throughput wor=
kloads, the 2 GB cap is increasingly a problem:
 * {*}Excessive file handle usage{*}: Each segment needs 4 files ({{{}.log{=
}}},=C2=A0{{{}.index{}}},=C2=A0{{{}.timeindex{}}},=C2=A0{{{}.txnindex{}}}).=
 A 10 TB partition with 2 GB segments means ~20,000 open files.
 * {*}Frequent segment rolls{*}: A topic ingesting 500 MB/s rolls a new seg=
ment every ~4 seconds, amplifying index build, flush, and cleaner overhead.
 * {*}More log cleaning / compaction work{*}: More segments means more comp=
action cycles with more small groups.
 * {*}Remote storage overhead{*}: Each segment is an individual unit for ti=
ered storage copy/delete operations.

Allowing segments of 4 GB, 8 GB, or larger would significantly reduce these=
 overheads for high-throughput, large-retention workloads.



