Hi Kirk,
Thanks for your response.

AS11: I tend to agree that admin clients have less interesting configuration.=
 But the KIP is a specification of the behaviour, so I think it should say, e=
specially since it does make a few references to admin clients such as having=
 the config to disable config push. If you do choose to have some default con=
figs for admin clients, client.id is the obvious one because it's pushed by a=
ll of the other kinds of clients.

AS12: Building on MM3, maybe we should have a compoundClientId for Kafka Stre=
ams, Kafka Connect, and so on. I avoided suggesting clientGroupId and groupIn=
stanceId because of the opportunity for confusion with existing concepts :)=20

Thanks,
Andrew

