> Hi Kafka community,
>=20
> We're organizing a hackathon at Community Over Code Glasgow 2026 =
(October 11=E2=80=9314) and Kafka has sessions on the schedule. We'd =
love for your community to participate.
>=20
> The idea is simple: dedicated time and space at the conference for =
contributors (new and existing) to work together on real tasks =E2=80=94 =
fixing bugs, writing docs, tackling issues that need focused attention, =
or onboarding new contributors.
>=20
> To participate, we'd need a few things from your project:
>    =E2=80=A2 A point of contact =E2=80=94 someone we can coordinate =
with on logistics and who'll be present at the event.
>    =E2=80=A2 A list of tasks =E2=80=94 bugs, docs, features, =
good-first-issues, or whatever your project wants to focus on. This =
helps people show up ready to contribute rather than spending the first =
hour figuring out what to work on.
>    =E2=80=A2 Promotion =E2=80=94 a message to your dev@ and users@ =
lists letting people know this is happening and encouraging them to =
attend.
>=20
> This is the first year we're bringing the hackathon back, so we're =
treating it as a pilot =E2=80=94 we want to gauge interest before =
committing to scale. Even if only a few contributors from your project =
can participate, that's a great start.
>=20
> If you're interested, please reply here or reach out to me directly. =
Even a quick "yes, we're in" or "maybe, let's talk" is helpful as we =
figure out how many projects to plan for.
>=20
> Also, please join us in the #hackathon channel on the ApacheCon Slack =
=E2=80=94 that's where we'll be coordinating as things come together: =
http://s.apache.org/apachecon-slack
>=20
> Thanks,
> Rich, on behalf of the Community Over Code planners


=E2=80=94=20
Rich Bowen
rbowen@rcbowen.com





