.createServerSideSslContextFactory(SSLUtils.java:60)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.runtime.rest.RestServer.cr=
eateConnector(RestServer.java:171)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.runtime.rest.RestServer.cr=
eateConnector(RestServer.java:144)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.runtime.rest.RestServer.cr=
eateConnectors(RestServer.java:124)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.runtime.rest.RestServer.<i=
nit>(RestServer.java:114)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.runtime.rest.ConnectRestSe=
rver.<init>(ConnectRestServer.java:39)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.cli.AbstractConnectCli.sta=
rtConnect(AbstractConnectCli.java:131)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.cli.AbstractConnectCli.run=
(AbstractConnectCli.java:95)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.cli.ConnectDistributed.mai=
n(ConnectDistributed.java:112)*

=C2=A0

=C2=A0

*Root cause*

KAFKA-19112 changed the default of ssl.cipher.suites from null to List.of()=
 in SslConfigs.addClientSslSupport(), and correspondingly changed the guard=
 in SSLUtils.configureSslContextFactoryAlgorithms() from:

=C2=A0 if (sslCipherSuites !=3D null)

=C2=A0 to:

=C2=A0 if (!sslCipherSuites.isEmpty())

This is safe when the config is resolved through the normal ConfigDef path.=
 However, SSLUtils resolves configs via {_}AbstractConfig.valuesWithPrefixA=
llOrNothing("listeners.https."){_}. This method has an "all or nothing" sem=
antic: if any _listeners.https.*_ prefixed property is set, it returns only=
 the prefixed entries without applying ConfigDef defaults for missing keys.

I'd expect most deployments to set some listener-prefixed SSL properties (i=
n our case, we set keystore & truststore) but rely on the default cipher su=
ites ({_}listeners.https.ssl.cipher.suites{_} is not set). This means the k=
ey is
=C2=A0 absent from the returned map, Map.get() returns null, and the .isEmp=
ty() call throws an NPE.


*To reproduce:*

=C2=A0 listeners=3Dhttp://0.0.0.0:8083,https://0.0.0.0:8084
=C2=A0 listeners.https.ssl.keystore.location=3D/path/to/keystore.jks
=C2=A0 listeners.https.ssl.keystore.password=3Dchangeit
=C2=A0 listeners.https.ssl.key.password=3Dchangeit
=C2=A0 listeners.https.ssl.truststore.location=3D/path/to/truststore.jks
=C2=A0 listeners.https.ssl.truststore.password=3Dchangeit

Starting the worker with these properties will fail immediately throwing th=
e NPE mentioned above=C2=A0



