> Connect REST server throws NPE on startup when using listener-prefixed SS=
L configs
> -------------------------------------------------------------------------=
---------
>
>                 Key: KAFKA-20572
>                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20572
>             Project: Kafka
>          Issue Type: Bug
>          Components: connect
>    Affects Versions: 4.2.0
>            Reporter: Hector Geraldino
>            Assignee: Ken Huang
>            Priority: Blocker
>             Fix For: 4.3.0, 4.2.1
>
>
> Kafka Connect fails to start with a NullPointerException when the worker =
configuration uses listener-prefixed SSL properties (e.g. listeners.https.s=
sl.keystore.location) but does not explicitly set listeners.https.ssl.ciphe=
r.suites.
> This is a regression introduced in KAFKA-19112 (PR #[20334|https://github=
.com/apache/kafka/pull/20334]).
> =C2=A0
> *Stack trace*
> {code:java}
> java.lang.NullPointerException: Cannot invoke "java.util.List.isEmpty()" =
because "sslCipherSuites" is null
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.runtime.rest.util.SSLUti=
ls.configureSslContextFactoryAlgorithms(SSLUtils.java:138)
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.runtime.rest.util.SSLUti=
ls.createServerSideSslContextFactory(SSLUtils.java:50)
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.runtime.rest.util.SSLUti=
ls.createServerSideSslContextFactory(SSLUtils.java:60)
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.runtime.rest.RestServer.=
createConnector(RestServer.java:171)
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.runtime.rest.RestServer.=
createConnector(RestServer.java:144)
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.runtime.rest.RestServer.=
createConnectors(RestServer.java:124)
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.runtime.rest.RestServer.=
<init>(RestServer.java:114)
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.runtime.rest.ConnectRest=
Server.<init>(ConnectRestServer.java:39)
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.cli.AbstractConnectCli.s=
tartConnect(AbstractConnectCli.java:131)
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.cli.AbstractConnectCli.r=
un(AbstractConnectCli.java:95)
> =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at org.apache.kafka.connect.cli.ConnectDistributed.m=
ain(ConnectDistributed.java:112){code}
> =C2=A0
> *Root cause*
> KAFKA-19112 changed the default of ssl.cipher.suites from null to List.of=
() in SslConfigs.addClientSslSupport(), and correspondingly changed the gua=
rd in SSLUtils.configureSslContextFactoryAlgorithms() from:
> =C2=A0 if (sslCipherSuites !=3D null)
> =C2=A0 to:
> =C2=A0 if (!sslCipherSuites.isEmpty())
> This is safe when the config is resolved through the normal ConfigDef pat=
h. However, SSLUtils resolves configs via {_}AbstractConfig.valuesWithPrefi=
xAllOrNothing("listeners.https."){_}. This method has an "all or nothing" s=
emantic: if any _listeners.https.*_ prefixed property is set, it returns on=
ly the prefixed entries without applying ConfigDef defaults for missing key=
s.
> I'd expect most deployments to set some listener-prefixed SSL properties =
(in our case, we set keystore & truststore) but rely on the default cipher =
suites ({_}listeners.https.ssl.cipher.suites{_} is not set). This means the=
 key is
> =C2=A0 absent from the returned map, Map.get() returns null, and the .isE=
mpty() call throws an NPE.
> =C2=A0
> *To reproduce:*
> {code:java}
>   listeners=3Dhttp://0.0.0.0:8083,https://0.0.0.0:8084
> =C2=A0 listeners.https.ssl.keystore.location=3D/path/to/keystore.jks
> =C2=A0 listeners.https.ssl.keystore.password=3Dchangeit
> =C2=A0 listeners.https.ssl.key.password=3Dchangeit
> =C2=A0 listeners.https.ssl.truststore.location=3D/path/to/truststore.jks
> =C2=A0 listeners.https.ssl.truststore.password=3Dchangeit{code}
> =C2=A0=C2=A0
> Starting the worker with these properties will fail immediately throwing =
the NPE mentioned above=C2=A0



