Chris,

Instead of increasing the hard-coded value to another bigger hard-coded val=
ue which might not work for some customers' environment or interfere with u=
nhealthy worker detection mechanism, I think it is better to have the timeo=
ut value explicitly defined as a configuration parameter.

So I created a new KIP-1339:=C2=A0Make KafkaConfigBackingStore read_write_t=
otal_timeout configurable (https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFK=
A/KIP-1339%3A+Make+KafkaConfigBackingStore+read_write_total_timeout+configu=
rable)

Please discuss on the discussion thread of the KIP (https://lists.apache.or=
g/thread/dl4wn0lsqly1glf49jd78rmslps9bktt)

Thanks.




On Friday, March 13, 2026 at 06:04:32 PM PDT, Henry Haiying Cai via dev <de=
v@kafka.apache.org> wrote:=20





The parameter for poll.interval is=C2=A0max.poll.interval.ms with the defau=
lt value of 300s. =C2=A0I can see 2 different ways of codings without intro=
ducing a KIP or some complex logic:

1. Increase the=C2=A0READ_WRITE_TOTAL_TIMEOUT_MS to a little bigger value e=
.g. 120s (which should still well under=C2=A0max.poll.interval.ms of 300s),=
 but if 120s is more than half of=C2=A0max.poll.interval.ms we should decre=
ase that value to 1/2 of max.poll.interval.ms.
2. Set=C2=A0READ_WRITE_TOTAL_TIMEOUT_MS =3D max(30s,=C2=A0max.poll.interval=
.ms / 2). (this will honor the existing setting of=C2=A0READ_WRITE_TOTAL_TI=
MEOUT_MS of at least 30s

I think option 2 is easier to understand.

More flexible way is to introduce a new config parameter for=C2=A0READ_WRIT=
E_TOTAL_TIMEOUT_MS but this needs a KIP


On Friday, March 13, 2026 at 06:32:28 AM PDT, Chris Egerton <fearthecellos@=
gmail.com> wrote:=20





I wonder if the optimal value would be related to the cluster settings? For=
 example, we could make it the expected poll interval (don't recall the nam=
e of the exact property, sorry!) minus 5 seconds, and then if a write fails=
 due to timeout, instruct users to increase the poll interval but note that=
 excessively large values for it may delay the detection of unhealthy worke=
rs in the cluster.

Does that sound reasonable?


On Fri, Mar 13, 2026, 02:59 Henry Haiying Cai <haiying_cai@yahoo.com> wrote=
:
> Thanks Chris for the quick reply.
>=20
> For the patch to increase the hard-coded value of=C2=A0READ_WRITE_TOTAL_T=
IMEOUT_MS, which value would be acceptable: 60s, 120s, 180s, 240s, 300s?
>=20
> In the meantime we will also try to increase the batch.size and linger.ms=
 for the producer.
>=20
>=20
>=20
> On Thursday, March 12, 2026 at 07:12:21 PM PDT, Chris Egerton <fearthecel=
los@gmail.com> wrote:=20
>=20
>=20
>=20
>=20
>=20
> Hi,
>=20
> I think it'd be fine to increase the hardcoded value in a patch PR. Makin=
g it configurable (possibly even as a function of the number of tasks?) wou=
ld be nice but we'd need a KIP to make that change.
>=20
> We can't make it too high, though, or the worker may fall out of the clus=
ter due to taking too long in between polls.
>=20
> For now, just as a temporary workaround, you (and anyone else running int=
o this) can possibly try tuning the producer config to use a non-zero linge=
r time, higher batch size, etc. in order to achieve higher throughout.
>=20
> Cheers,=C2=A0
>=20
> On Thu, Mar 12, 2026, 22:03 Henry Haiying Cai via dev <dev@kafka.apache.o=
rg> wrote:
>> Hi kafka-connect folks,
>>=20
>> READ_WRITE_TOTAL_TIMEOUT_MS is currently hardcoded as 30 second in kafka=
-connect's=C2=A0KafkaConfigBackingStore.java (https://github.com/a0x8o/kafk=
a/blob/master/connect/runtime/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/connect/storag=
e/KafkaConfigBackingStore.java#L244).=C2=A0 This parameter is used to contr=
ol the upper bound time we allowed to write configuration changes to the ka=
fka-connect's config.storage topic (and this topic is usually configured as=
 one-partition topic)
>>=20
>> We have topics with more than 500 partitions and the connector tasks of =
more than 500 (one task for each kafka partition).=C2=A0 When the consumer =
rebalance happens, kafka-connect code needs to finish the writing of all ta=
sk configs into the config.storage topic within=C2=A0READ_WRITE_TOTAL_TIMEO=
UT_MS and sometimes it is not enough time.
>>=20
>> Can we increase=C2=A0READ_WRITE_TOTAL_TIMEOUT_MS to a larger value e.g. =
300 seconds?=C2=A0 Or better to make it a configurable parameter?
>>=20
>=20
>=20


