>
>
> [https://develocity.apache.org/scans/tests?search.buildToolType=3Dgradle&=
search.relativeStartTime=3DP28D&search.rootProjectNames=3Dkafka&search.time=
ZoneId=3DAsia%2FCalcutta&tests.container=3Dorg.apache.kafka.clients.consume=
r.ShareConsumerRackAwareTest&tests.test=3DtestShareConsumerWithRackAwareAss=
ignor(ClusterInstance)%5B1%5D]
> Preliminary analysis:
> =C2=A0
> =C2=A0
> =C2=A0 1. Test calls alterPartitionReassignments to move partitions betwe=
en brokers/racks.
> =C2=A0 2. During the transition, a share group heartbeat fires. Share gro=
ups have an extra trigger =E2=80=94 initializedAssignmentPending()
> =C2=A0 (GroupMetadataManager.java) =E2=80=94 that forces assignment recom=
putation on every heartbeat when there are unassigned initialized partition=
s. Combined
> =C2=A0 with SHARE_GROUP_ASSIGNMENT_INTERVAL_MS_CONFIG=3D0, this means eve=
ry heartbeat triggers the assignor.
> =C2=A0 3. The RackAwareAssignor runs against transitional metadata where =
a partition's rack set doesn't match any member. It throws PartitionAssigno=
rException.
> =C2=A0[2026-05-10 21:15:09,514] ERROR [GroupCoordinator id=3D0] Operation=
 share-group-heartbeat with ShareGroupHeartbeatRequestData(groupId=3D'group=
0', memberId=3D'mMvKOe5MR0aBoDlFTKTTnA', memberEpoch=3D10, rackId=3Dnull, s=
ubscribedTopicNames=3Dnull) hit an unexpected exception: org.apache.kafka.c=
ommon.errors.UnknownServerException: Failed to compute a new target assignm=
ent for epoch 11: No member found for racks [rack2] for partition 0 of topi=
c TDeVaIP_Q2OWvedEfXl_ng. (org.apache.kafka.coordinator.group.GroupCoordina=
torService:54)=09
> java.util.concurrent.CompletionException: org.apache.kafka.common.errors.=
UnknownServerException: Failed to compute a new target assignment for epoch=
 11: No member found for racks [rack2] for partition 0 of topic TDeVaIP_Q2O=
WvedEfXl_ng
> =C2=A0 4. GroupMetadataManager.maybeUpdateTargetAssignment wraps it as Un=
knownServerException.
> =C2=A0 5. AbstractHeartbeatRequestManager treats this as a fatal error, t=
ransitioning the consumer member to FATAL state permanently.
> =C2=A0 6. On test teardown, ShareConsumerImpl.close() tries to leave the =
group, encounters the UnknownServerException in the background event queue,=
 and throws KafkaException("Failed to close Kafka share consumer").



