> AS11: I tend to agree that admin clients have less interesting configu=
ration. But the KIP is a specification of the behaviour, so I think it s=
hould say, especially since it does make a few references to admin clien=
ts such as having the config to disable config push. If you do choose to=
 have some default configs for admin clients, client.id is the obvious o=
ne because it's pushed by all of the other kinds of clients.

I will add defaults for Admin client, but I expect most users will want =
to disable the collection of admin configs.

> AS12: Building on MM3, maybe we should have a compoundClientId for Kaf=
ka Streams, Kafka Connect, and so on. I avoided suggesting clientGroupId=
 and groupInstanceId because of the opportunity for confusion with exist=
ing concepts :)=20

Yes, a meta ID to link the top level client with embedded clients is sti=
ll lacking in the KIP. I'll focus on this for the next revision.

Thanks,
Kirk

