Hello Jun, chia,

I've updated KIP-1327 with a design change based on the discussion=20
feedback.=20

The updated design decouples the new-partition reset behavior from=20
the base auto.offset.reset policy:=20

- auto.offset.reset.max.age.ms now applies to all auto.offset.reset =
values=20
(latest, earliest, by_duration, none).=20
- For new ("hot") partitions, the consumer resets to =
auto.offset.reset.new.partitions=20
config setting
- For existing ("cold") partitions, the base auto.offset.reset policy =
continues=20
to apply unchanged.=20
- The new-partition reset behavior is represented by a separate internal =
config=20
(auto.offset.reset.new.partitions, currently fixed to earliest). This =
decoupled design makes=20
it straightforward to promote the behavior to a public user-facing =
configuration in a future KIP.

Best Regards,
Jiunn-Yang


