------------------------------------

             Summary: Kafka Streams issue
                 Key: KAFKA-20594
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20594
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
    Affects Versions: 3.4.0
            Reporter: Aayush Gupta


Looking for some=C2=A0Kafka=C2=A0Streams=C2=A0expertise on an issue we're i=
nvestigating.

Problem: A=C2=A0KafkaStreams-based consumer stops polling after ~15 minutes=
 of topic inactivity. The adapter stays alive, but no messages are picked u=
p until it's manually restarted. Reproduces on both IBM MQ-backed=C2=A0Kafk=
a=C2=A0and Confluent Cloud.

Suspected cause: Back-to-back expiry of=C2=A0[connections.max.idle.ms|http:=
//connections.max.idle.ms/]=C2=A0(client, 9 min default) + broker idle time=
out (~10 min). Stream thread dies on the next poll attempt,=C2=A0KafkaStrea=
ms goes to ERROR state silently =E2=80=94 no StateListener or UncaughtExcep=
tionHandler was registered, so nothing recovers.

Questions:

Is this a known pattern with=C2=A0KafkaStreams on idle topics? Any recommen=
ded approach?
Is the close() + re-instantiate pattern safe? Any rebalance/duplicate risks=
?
For=C2=A0Kafka=C2=A02.8+, should we prefer StreamsUncaughtExceptionHandler =
with REPLACE_THREAD instead of a full restart?
Any input appreciated!



Not observing any error stacks or exceptions in the logs when the issue occ=
urs.
As part of our investigation, we wanted to check if there are any JVM flags=
 or framework-level configurations=C2=A0that can be enabled to extract more=
 detailed=C2=A0Kafka=C2=A0framework debug logs, particularly around=C2=A0Ka=
fka=C2=A0Streams and consumer lifecycle behavior.


Given the absence of exceptions or diagnostic logs, it is unclear whether f=
urther tuning of=C2=A0Kafka=C2=A0consumer properties alone would meaningful=
ly alleviate the issue without better visibility into the=C2=A0Kafka=C2=A0S=
treams internals.
>From your experience, do you have any recommendations beyond enabling more =
detailed=C2=A0Kafka/Streams logging=E2=80=94such as known patterns, specifi=
c stream-thread behaviors, or client-side recovery considerations=E2=80=94t=
hat we should be exploring in parallel?
Any guidance would be greatly appreciated.



