Hi all,

Adding on a couple more points for motivation:

1. Users typically set MDC context from each record but this can break =
in subtle ways for both sync/async threading models

for (var r: consumer.poll(=E2=80=A6)) {
    MDC.put(=E2=80=9Ckafka.offset=E2=80=9D, r.offset());=20
    // add rest of the fields
    process(r); // throws an ex
    MDC.clear();
}

In both sync and async models, record N+1 carries prev record=E2=80=99s =
context during exceptions. The solution is a try finally for cleanup, =
yet more boilerplate for teams to maintain manually. Across thread =
boundaries, we have to manually copy threadlocals around from the poller =
loop (such as OTel,DD spans).

In KafkaShareConsumer, this behaviour is more common when worker threads =
can perform individual redelivery, ack calls. Sometimes, a main poll =
loop for try/catch does not neatly cleanup state between records.

2. I also see Confluent=E2=80=99s parallel-consumer implement a =
PollContext to achieve a similar function to wrap each poll() action =
per-record.

Best,
Aditya

