> To make this work for KIP-714/KIP-1076, we would need to change the=20
> client APIs a little bit, and allow Kafka Streams to pass it's own UUID=20
> into the consumer/admin client to be use to push the Streams metrics. We=20
> would also need to expose the Streams clientInstanceID via the=20
> `ClientInstanceIds` interface.
>=20
> For KIP-1324 and KIP-1331, we would need similar APIs.
>=20
> I don't think we can (atm) unify this with KIP-848/1071 member-ID=20
> though, as a Kafka Streams client has multiple threads, and each thread=20
