Hi, Andrew,

Thanks for the reply.

JR23. Our message protocol doc says "Any fields in the message object that
are not present in the version that you are deserializing will be reset to
default values.  Unless a custom default has been set:". Uuid fields
default to zero uuid.
So if the server gets header.clientInstanceId=3D0 in the deserialized heade=
r,
could it distinguish between the ID not being present (since client is old)
and the ID being explicitly set to 0 by the client?

Jun


