Hi Rajini,

RS13: Updated.

RS14: Updated.

RS15: Agreed. Renamed to mirror.state.topic.num.partitions and
mirror.state.topic.replication.factor.

RS16: The destination is treated as a full replica of the source's ACL
state. There is no concept of "destination=E2=80=91only" ACLs (except for
CLUSTER_MIRROR resource type ACLs, which are explicitly skipped). A
DENY ACL created directly on the destination would be wiped on the
next sync cycle. That said, you can always use mirror.acl.include
configuration to alter this behavior.

RS17: Correct, updated.

Thanks
Fede


