Hi,

At the moment Apache Kafka has not adopted project specific guidelines.
You should just follow the Apache Software Foundation guidelines:
https://www.apache.org/legal/generative-tooling.html

Thanks,
Mickael

On Wed, May 20, 2026 at 8:43=E2=80=AFAM Aldan Basil Brito (Nokia) via dev
<dev@kafka.apache.org> wrote:
>
> Hi Community,
>
> I would like to start a discussion on the use of AI-assisted tools for co=
de generation within the project development workflow.
> With the increasing adoption of AI-based development tools (for example, =
code assistants and IDE integrations), it would be helpful to understand th=
e community's position on:
>
>   *   Whether the use of AI-assisted code generation is acceptable for co=
ntributions to the project.
>   *   Any expectations around review, validation, or attribution of AI-ge=
nerated code.
>   *   Recommended guidelines or best practices contributors should follow=
 when using such tools.
>   *   Any licensing, security, or provenance considerations the community=
 would like contributors to be aware of.
>
> The intention is to ensure that any use of AI tools aligns with Apache co=
mmunity standards, code quality expectations, and project governance practi=
ces.
> Looking forward to the community's feedback and guidance on this topic.
>
> Thanks & Regards,
> Aldan
>

