hi TaIju

Could you flesh out the motivation for using =E2=80=9CLeaderOnly=E2=80=9D in=
stead of =E2=80=9Cacks=E2=80=9D? We could use acks at the RPC level to maint=
ain flexibility, while the Java APIs can remain strict on using a boolean.

Best,
Chia-Ping

> TaiJu Wu <tjwu1217@gmail.com> =E6=96=BC 2026=E5=B9=B45=E6=9C=8820=E6=97=A5=
 =E6=99=9A=E4=B8=8A9:21 =E5=AF=AB=E9=81=93=EF=BC=9A
>=20
> =EF=BB=BFHi team,
>=20
> I would like to discuss KIP-1343: Allow opt-in leader-only acknowledgement=

> in DeleteRecords
> to enable async deleteRecords RPC.
>=20
> KIP:
> https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1343%3A+Allow+opt-in=
+leader-only+acknowledgement+in+DeleteRecords
>=20
> Thanks,
> TaiJuWu

