This is very interesting feature that we've lacked in our org and faced its
consequences many times.
I believe this can improve a lot of stability in our kafka clusters.

On 2025/07/31 12:16:31 mapan wrote:
> Hi all,
>
> I=E2=80=99d like to start a discussion about a new KIP:
> https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/x/Nw9JFg
>
> This KIP suggests adding disk threshold configs in Kafka and rejecting ne=
w
> product
> requests after reaching the threshold to prevent disk full failure.
>
> This strategy is similar to RocketMQ's diskMaxUsedSpaceRatio config or
> RabbitMQ's
> disk_free_limit config, and I hope to implement this strategy in our
> environment.
>
> Please share your feedback, questions, or concerns so we can refine
> the proposal together.
>
> Best regards,
> mapan
>

