> > > > > FV1:  The proposal does not specify what happens when multiple AC=
Ls
> > > > > with overlapping CIDR ranges apply to the same request. CIDR
> > > > > introduces a new dimension: subnet specificity. The KIP should
> > clarify
> > > > > whether longest-prefix match apply, or whether CIDR ranges are
> > treated
> > > > > like wildcards. Without this, users will create overlapping rules
> > with
> > > > > unpredictable results.
> > > > >
> > > > > For example:
> > > > > - ALLOW 10.0.0.0/8 on topic foo
> > > > > - DENY 10.0.1.0/24 on topic foo
