Edoardo Comar created KAFKA-20619:
-------------------------------------

             Summary: ClusterTests may report Thread leak detected: Cleaner=
-0, Cleaner-1
                 Key: KAFKA-20619
                 URL: https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/KAFKA-20619
             Project: Kafka
          Issue Type: Bug
          Components: unit tests
            Reporter: Edoardo Comar


Running in today's trunk (commit
89f3888c8718da91967badef560cf34ebe8e09ed)=C2=A0

A test like=C2=A0
./gradlew clean client:clients-integration-tests:test --tests SocketServerM=
emoryPoolTest

I get consistently

testProduceRequestWithUnsupportedVersion [1] Type=3DRaft-Combined, Metadata=
Version=3D4.4-IV0,BrokerSecurityProtocol=3DPLAINTEXT,BrokerListenerName=3DL=
istenerName(EXTERNAL),ControllerSecurityProtocol=3DPLAINTEXT,ControllerList=
enerName=3DListenerName(CONTROLLER) FAILED
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 org.opentest4j.AssertionFailedError: Thread leak detected: Cl=
eaner-0, Cleaner-1 =3D=3D> expected: <true> but was: <false>
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at app//org.apache.kafka.common.test.junit.Clus=
terTestExtensions.afterEach(ClusterTestExtensions.java:184)
=C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 =C2=A0 at java.base@21.0.10/java.util.Optional.ifPrese=
nt(Optional.java:178)


Which appears to be due to (Claude's report)

Root cause =E2=80=94 Cleaner-0 / Cleaner-1 are JDK-internal daemon threads =
created lazily by jdk.internal.ref.CleanerImpl (group: InnocuousThreadGroup=
). They're not
=C2=A0 application threads; they're spawned by JDK code for native resource=
 cleanup (e.g. direct ByteBuffer deallocation) and live in the InnocuousThr=
eadGroup. The
=C2=A0 ClusterTestExtensions thread-leak detector doesn't currently skip th=
em, so it flags them as leaks.

=C2=A0 Why now =E2=80=94 they're triggered the first time the broker happen=
s to allocate enough direct-buffer-backed objects whose cleanup uses
=C2=A0 jdk.internal.ref.CleanerFactory. The testRequestWithUnsupportedVersi=
on path goes through processChannelException which logs a full stack trace =
via log4j2 =E2=80=94
=C2=A0 log4j2's formatting / reflective stack walk can be what causes the J=
DK to spin up these cleaners on first use. The corrupt-body test runs secon=
d, so by
=C2=A0 beforeEach the cleaners already exist and aren't reported as "new".



