Hi all,

Friendly bump on this vote thread. With the KIP freeze for 4.4 approaching
in early June, it would be great if you could take a moment to review and
vote.

To recap, this KIP adds subnet-level support (CIDR notation) to ACL host
patterns, so administrators can write rules for entire IP ranges instead of
maintaining individual entries per host.

Related KIP: https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1276
Discussion:
https://lists.apache.org/thread/4o5lcl2nbzt0sf28rzx90rnyyf50xfx2

Thanks,
Maros

