Hi Matthias,
Thanks for your thoughtful response.

You are entirely correct about the member ID being a string for the group pro=
tocols and the clientInstanceId being a UUID in the protocol. The Java client=
 and librdkafka do not use the same string encoding for the member ID, even t=
hough they both use a UUID on the client. librdkafka of course does not use J=
ava UUID code.

The "nightmare" that I referred to in the comments is that we would end up wi=
th RPC versions which depend upon the presence of a tagged field in the reque=
st header, and not something more concrete such as a version bump of the requ=
est header itself. Tagged fields are by their very nature intended to be opti=
onal, so I really do not like requiring a tagged field in the request header =
as part of the contract of potential new versions of GetTelemetrySubscription=
s and PushTelemetry. It seems to me that the versioning in the Kafka protocol=
 is not supposed to depend upon something as unreliable as the presence of an=
 optional field. Your mileage may vary, of course. This is why the presence o=
f the tagged field in KIP-1313 is conditional. If there's a clientInstanceId,=
 these are the rules.

It is also abundantly clear that the local client concept needs quite a lot o=
f alignment before we could get an agreed spec for a KIP.

Thanks,
Andrew

