Subject: [VOTE] KIP-1320: Deprecate Utils, ByteBufferInputStream, and
 ByteBufferOutputStream and introduce internal replacements
To: dev@kafka.apache.org
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="UTF-8"
From: Eric Chang <unknowntpo@apache.org>
Reply-To: <dev@kafka.apache.org>

Hi Kafka devs,

I would like to call a vote for KIP-1320:

https://cwiki.apache.org/confluence/display/KAFKA/KIP-1320%3A+Deprecate+%60Utils%60%2C+%60ByteBufferInputStream%60%2C+and+%60ByteBufferOutputStream%60+and+introduce+internal+replacements

Discussion thread:
https://lists.apache.org/thread/5hf11khclhngftp297hhvwc23j5bcx28

This KIP proposes to deprecate `org.apache.kafka.common.utils.Utils`,
`org.apache.kafka.common.utils.ByteBufferInputStream`, and
`org.apache.kafka.common.utils.ByteBufferOutputStream` in Kafka `4.4.0`,
introduce copied replacements under `org.apache.kafka.common.utils.internals`
for Kafka internal usage, and remove the old classes in Kafka `5.0.0`.

Thanks,
Eric Chang

