Hi all,

Following up here on further discussion in code review. In the last design, w=
e proposed to make all methods with a default empty body.  This breaks sourc=
e compatibility for Scala requiring an override def.=20

To address this, I=E2=80=99ve changed the design slightly that will position=
 the improvement a bit better. I=E2=80=99ve introduced a new super interface=
 RebalanceListener with exactly the same shape as ConsumerRebalanceListener b=
ut with the extra parameter RebalanceConsumer. The existing interface will s=
imply extend it overriding with defaults to the 1-arg methods . We also mark=
 ConsumerRebalanceListener as deprecated.

Relatedly the set method on Consumer will be setRebalanceListener.=20

In light of this major change, I wanted to re-open the vote so that everyone=
 is onboard with the proposed changes.=20

Do let me know your thoughts.

GitHub discussion: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/22270#discussion_r33=
12040954
